---
import StandardPageLayout from "../../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro";
import PageToc from "../../components/PageToc.astro";
import "../../styles/standards-poster.css";
import "../../styles/extended.css";
import metadata from "../../data/standards/japangaap/asbj06.json";
---

<StandardPageLayout
  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  description={metadata.summary}
  issued={metadata.issued}
  latestAmendment={metadata.latestAmendment}
  status={metadata.status}
  summary={metadata.summary}
  bannerNotice={metadata.bannerNotice}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "Conceptual Framework Linkage" },
        { id: "s2", label: "Scope" },
        { id: "s3", label: "Replacing the Old Statement of Appropriation of Retained Earnings" },
        { id: "s4", label: "Structure — Tracking Every Net Assets Component" },
        { id: "s5", label: "Detailed Movement Analysis for Shareholders' Equity" },
        { id: "s6", label: "Aggregate Movement for Other Net Assets Components" },
        { id: "s7", label: "Worked Example — a Shareholders' Equity Movement Schedule" },
        { id: "s8", label: "Worked Example — Reflecting a Dividend and a Share Issuance" },
        { id: "s9", label: "Disclosure Requirements" },
        { id: "s10", label: "Critical Judgments" },
        { id: "s11", label: "Relationship to IAS/IFRS" },
        { id: "s12", label: "Statement Mapping" },
        { id: "s13", label: "Related Standards" },
        { id: "s14", label: "Glossary" }
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>

  <div class="wrap">

    <div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">The primary statement tracking how Net Assets moved during the period</div>
        <div class="principle">ASBJ Statement No. 6 establishes the Statement of Changes in Net Assets (株主資本等変動計算書, literally "statement of changes in shareholders' equity, etc.") as ONE of the primary financial statements REQUIRED under J-GAAP — presenting HOW each component of the Net Assets (純資産) section established by ASBJ Statement No. 5 CHANGED during the reporting period, connecting the OPENING and CLOSING Balance Sheet positions with a clear account of what drove the movement.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Scope</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">All companies preparing a full set of J-GAAP financial statements</div>
        <div class="principle">This Statement applies to ALL companies preparing financial statements under J-GAAP, requiring the Statement of Changes in Net Assets as a MANDATORY primary statement alongside the Balance Sheet and Statement of Income.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>Replacing the Old Statement of Appropriation of Retained Earnings</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">A shift from a single annual appropriation event to continuous, comprehensive tracking</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">Before this Statement, Japanese practice centred around a SEPARATE "Statement of Appropriation of Retained Earnings" (利益処分計算書) — reflecting the OLDER governance model where dividend and reserve decisions were formally APPROVED as a discrete event at the shareholders' general meeting. As Japan's Companies Act evolved to permit MORE FLEXIBLE, ongoing capital transactions (share issuances, treasury share transactions, interim dividends), the OLD single-event appropriation statement became INADEQUATE — the Statement of Changes in Net Assets REPLACED it with a COMPREHENSIVE, CONTINUOUS presentation covering ALL Net Assets movements during the period, not just the annual profit appropriation decision.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>Structure — Tracking Every Net Assets Component</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Opening balance, movements during the period, closing balance — for each of the four parts</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">The Statement presents, for EACH of the four Net Assets components established by ASBJ Statement No. 5 (Shareholders' Equity, Valuation and Translation Adjustments, Subscription Rights to Shares, and Non-controlling Interests): the OPENING balance at the start of the period, the MOVEMENTS occurring DURING the period, and the resulting CLOSING balance — reconciling directly to the Balance Sheet's Net Assets figures at both dates.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>Detailed Movement Analysis for Shareholders' Equity</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Each sub-component's own movement columns</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">For SHAREHOLDERS' EQUITY specifically, the Statement provides GRANULAR movement detail SEPARATELY for Common Stock, Capital Surplus, Retained Earnings, and Treasury Shares — showing individual line items such as NEW share issuances, DIVIDENDS paid, NET profit for the period (transferred into Retained Earnings), and TREASURY SHARE acquisitions/disposals — giving readers a genuinely TRANSPARENT account of exactly what drove each Shareholders' Equity sub-component's change.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>Aggregate Movement for Other Net Assets Components</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Generally a net change, unless material detail is warranted</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">For Valuation and Translation Adjustments, Subscription Rights to Shares, and Non-controlling Interests, the Statement TYPICALLY presents the NET change during the period as a SINGLE line, rather than the SAME granular, multi-line detail required for Shareholders' Equity — reflecting that these components generally involve FEWER, less frequently occurring transaction TYPES.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s7"><span class="num">7</span><h2>Worked Example — a Shareholders' Equity Movement Schedule</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Reconciling opening to closing balances</div>
        <div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: Retained Earnings movement for the year</div><div class="wk-body">A company's Retained Earnings opening balance is ¥3,200,000,000. During the year, it recognises net profit of ¥600,000,000 and pays dividends of ¥180,000,000.</div><div class="wk-answer">Retained Earnings closing balance = ¥3,200,000,000 + ¥600,000,000 (net profit) − ¥180,000,000 (dividends) = <strong>¥3,620,000,000</strong> — with EACH of these two movements shown as a SEPARATE, clearly labelled line in the Statement of Changes in Net Assets, reconciling directly to the Balance Sheet's Retained Earnings balance at year end.</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s8"><span class="num">8</span><h2>Worked Example — Reflecting a Dividend and a Share Issuance</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Multiple Shareholders' Equity components moving simultaneously</div>
        <div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: A new share issuance alongside the annual dividend</div><div class="wk-body">During the year, a company issues new shares raising ¥500,000,000 (¥250,000,000 credited to Common Stock, ¥250,000,000 to Capital Surplus), and pays ¥180,000,000 of dividends from Retained Earnings.</div><div class="wk-answer">The Statement shows: Common Stock INCREASING by ¥250,000,000 (new share issuance); Capital Surplus INCREASING by ¥250,000,000 (new share issuance); and Retained Earnings DECREASING by ¥180,000,000 (dividends) — each Shareholders' Equity sub-component's movement CLEARLY separately identified, rather than presented as one blended total change.</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s9"><span class="num">9</span><h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">What ASBJ Statement No. 6 requires</div><div class="check-list"><span>Opening and closing balances for each Net Assets component</span><span>Detailed line-item movements for each Shareholders' Equity sub-component</span><span>Net movement for Valuation and Translation Adjustments, Subscription Rights, and Non-controlling Interests</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s10"><span class="num">10</span><h2>Critical Judgments</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cn span2"><div class="ctitle cn">Where judgement matters most</div>
        <div class="two-col"><div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGEMENTS</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Appropriate level of disaggregation for movements that don't fit neatly into a single standard line item</span></div></div>
        <div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Generally minimal — this Statement is a presentational standard reflecting amounts already determined under other standards</span></div></div></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s11"><span class="num">11</span><h2>Relationship to IAS/IFRS</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Comparison — J-GAAP vs IFRS</div>
        <div class="td-table"><div class="th cols-12-12-12"><span>Feature</span><span>J-GAAP (ASBJ Statement No. 6)</span><span>IFRS (IAS 1)</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-12-12-12"><span>Mandatory primary statement</span><span>YES — Statement of Changes in Net Assets</span><span>YES — Statement of Changes in Equity, converged in overall purpose</span></div>
          <div class="tr alt cols-12-12-12"><span>Level of movement detail</span><span>Granular for Shareholders' Equity sub-components; aggregate for other Net Assets parts</span><span>Similarly granular for share capital/reserves, though specific column structure varies by entity</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="note">This is a genuinely CONVERGED area — both frameworks require a comprehensive, continuous statement of equity/net assets movements, reflecting a shared move AWAY from older, single-event profit appropriation-style reporting.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s12"><span class="num">12</span><h2>Statement Mapping</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Where every Net Assets movement lands</div>
        <div class="td-table"><div class="th cols-16-1-14"><span>Event</span><span>Statement(s) affected</span><span>Notes</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-16-1-14"><span>Any Net Assets component change</span><span><span class="badge be">SCNA</span> <span class="badge bs">BS</span></span><span>Tracked in the SCNA, reconciling to the Balance Sheet</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s13"><span class="num">13</span><h2>Related Standards</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
        <div class="td-table"><div class="th cols-08-2"><span>Standard</span><span>Connection</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-08-2"><span>ASBJ Statement No. 5</span><span>Supplies the four-part Net Assets structure this Statement tracks the movement of</span></div>
          <div class="tr alt cols-08-2"><span>ASBJ Statement No. 1</span><span>Supplies the treasury share and legal reserve movements commonly presented within this Statement</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s14"><span class="num">14</span><h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cn span2">
        <div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Statement of Changes in Net Assets (株主資本等変動計算書)</div><div class="glossary-def">The primary financial statement presenting the period-over-period movement in each Net Assets component.</div></div>
        <div class="glossary-item glossary-item--last"><div class="glossary-term">Statement of Appropriation of Retained Earnings (利益処分計算書) — legacy term</div><div class="glossary-def">The former statement presenting a single annual profit appropriation event, replaced by the more comprehensive Statement of Changes in Net Assets.</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="legend"><div class="ltitle">Financial statement key (Japan GAAP terminology)</div><div class="lrow"><span class="badge bs">BS</span> Balance Sheet (貸借対照表) <span class="badge bp">P&amp;L</span> Statement of Income / Profit and Loss Statement (損益計算書) <span class="badge bo">Net Assets</span> 純資産の部 <span class="badge be">SCNA</span> Statement of Changes in Net Assets (株主資本等変動計算書) <span class="badge bc">SCF</span> Statement of Cash Flows (キャッシュ・フロー計算書)</div></div>

  </div>
</StandardPageLayout>
